{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "0b8f2d4e-6a1c-47d3-9f5e-8c2a1b7d4e60"/*SendToOutput*/,
  "Description": "Supplies a texture to the project's active output setup.\n\nRouting lives in the setup, not on this op: the setup holds a content source standing 1:1 with this node, slices cut rectangles from it, and surfaces name the slice they show. So one render can be sliced across many surfaces without this op knowing about any of them.\n\nThis is a sink: it needs no output connection.\n\nAKA: corner pin, perspective, map, warp, projector output, send, sink, slice, atlas",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "1a50c781-1a20-4736-9ec4-60ff2254a537"/*ExposeToParents*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 300.0
      },
      "Description": "Makes this send visible to parent compositions when it sits inside a nested composition."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "1d83a6f2-49c0-4e17-8b5d-c72e90fa4b36"/*Color*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 135.0
      }
    },
    {
      "InputId": "3125e84e-8644-46a9-8fae-e88ed06731f4"/*ResolutionFrom*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 270.0
      },
      "Description": "Where the render size comes from. Surface Aspect: the proportions of the surface or region showing this content, at the height it would render at anyway (the Resolution Override's, or the output's when that is 0×0); it doesn't change while the surface is aligned, so feedback keeps running. Projected Surface: those proportions at a pixel per output pixel where the surface is projected densest, so nothing is upscaled; it follows the alignment and changes while points are moved. A [Layer2d] fills either without distortion. Output: the Resolution Override, or the size of the output this content is routed to when that is 0×0. For a render through the projector's own camera ([UseProjectorCam]), which fills the whole output."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "fd8d094d-dd51-4659-8aab-ca9a028bee33"/*ResolutionFactor*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 345.0
      },
      "Description": "Scales a size this op works out on its own: the surface's size, or the output's size while Resolution Override is 0×0. 0.5 renders at half size for heavy content, 2 renders sharper fine text. A Resolution Override you type in is used exactly.",
      "Min": 0.25,
      "Max": 2.0,
      "ClampMin": true
    },
    {
      "InputId": "3c7f1e58-0a94-4d62-b8f3-2e5d9a0c4b17"/*ResolutionOverride*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 225.0
      },
      "Description": "Renders at exactly this size, whatever Resolution From says (except Projected Surface). 0×0 leaves the size to Resolution From."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "8a4dd1b3-2e6f-4c25-9d0a-7f3b61c8e942"/*Texture*/,
      "Relevancy": "Required",
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      }
    },
    {
      "InputId": "9a1c4f7e-2d38-4b6a-8e50-1f7c3d9b0a24"/*Update*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": -200.0,
        "Y": 180.0
      }
    }
  ],
  "SymbolChildUis": [],
  "OutputUis": []
}